  "id": "COMPOUND:18170 - PROTEIN:3897",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc117493 and the cholesteryl ester transfer protein (CETP) through multiple indirect pathways. Pathway 1 links Npc117493 to HCT-8, which is targeted by a compound named 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol, which in turn targets CETP. Pathway 2 connects Npc117493 to ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, which is targeted by Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin, also targeting CETP. Pathway 3 links Npc117493 to HCT-8, which is targeted by methyl (Z)-pentadec-8-enoate, which also targets CETP. These pathways collectively indicate that Npc117493 may interact with compounds that ultimately influence CETP activity. The evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, suggesting a possible functional relationship between Npc117493 and CETP through the action of various compounds. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the final scores are relatively similar across the different paths, but the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain without further experimental validation.",
